        history:"Our Journey", objectives:"Objectives", values:"Core Values", transparency:"Transparency & Responsible Use of Funds", transparencyCopy:"The organization works to direct support toward educational, skill-development, environmental, women’s empowerment, and community welfare initiatives. Registration and compliance information is shared for transparency. Contributions are intended to support the stated social objectives responsibly.",
        presidentRole:"President / Chairperson", presidentName:"Vandana (Vedika) Pramod Sonawane", presidentIntro:"Writer, poet, public speaker, counselor, and social worker with experience in event management, business and community initiatives. She is committed to educational development in neglected and rural areas, environmental awareness through “Plant Trees, Save Trees,” personality development, and children’s overall development.",
        socialDebt:"“Everyone should strive to repay their social debt.”", presidentMessageHeading:"President’s Message", presidentMessage:"My inspiration came from my father’s habit of helping poor and needy families. Through my interaction with blind and disabled individuals, I began a social-service journey and visited various organizations to understand community needs.\n\nDuring rural visits, I became involved with children at the Zilla Parishad School in Dehane village, Bhimashankar. Work there began around 2016 through group contributions, with support from journalist Mr. Tamboli and the school teaching staff. The conditions faced by tribal children strengthened our commitment to rural education.\n\nWith a committed group and the valuable help of Shri Vijay Salunke in establishment and documentation, the name Dwarkamai was selected and the Sanstha was formally established on 20 June 2022. Since then, our work has included educational support, water filters, sports support, an environmental pledge, and expanded community initiatives. Accenture has also supported activities through CSR funding.",
        futureVisionHeading:"President’s Future Vision", futureVision:"To strengthen education in remote valleys and hilly areas; support school needs and personality development; provide girls’ self-defense; encourage environmental balance, waste management, cleanliness, tree plantation and awareness in villages; and advance women’s empowerment, economic development, and progressive villages.",
